{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing","id":1473884,"title":"Is Havesh the Vanisher still a thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-02T19:38:32-08:00","id":1473884,"title":"Is Havesh the Vanisher still a thing?","content":"In 3E, the UCS picks all Solars who exalt. Does that mean there are still evil Solars running around who kill random men, steal their identity, and sleep with their wives? Is Sol\u2019s hands clean in this regard, or does he dispassionately choose the people who are best suited to the task of wielding the power of an Exaltation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T01:11:49-08:00","id":1473890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing#post1473884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3E, the UCS picks all Solars who exalt. Does that mean there are still evil Solars running around who kill random men, steal their identity, and sleep with their wives? Is Sol\u2019s hands clean in this regard, or does he dispassionately choose the people who are best suited to the task of wielding the power of an Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't take my word for it, but i think that while Havesh has been cited, his character has seen something of a reworking in the process, focusing on him as more of figure contesting Varangian caste system laws and exploiting the unseen but all too present resentment in some parts, mainly among the lower castes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T13:46:13-08:00","id":1473927,"title":"","content":"Thanks, he was one of my favorite characters to hate back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T11:23:48-07:00","id":1505343,"title":"","content":"I don't think we should be too hard on the Sun for picking Havesh. (He deserves flack for abandoning Creation instead!)<br /> <br /> He isn't the Maidens, so he presumably can't predict the future all that well. He can look into a person's heart as they are right now, but he doesn't interview them to ask what specific actions they'll take if he gives them power. To some extent, I think he (and everyone who isn't the Maidens) has to just trust. Sometimes, you get Lyta or Havesh, but sometimes you get Harmonious Jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T12:51:18-07:00","id":1505361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing#post1473884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3E, the UCS picks all Solars who exalt. Does that mean there are still evil Solars running around who kill random men, steal their identity, and sleep with their wives? Is Sol\u2019s hands clean in this regard, or does he dispassionately choose the people who are best suited to the task of wielding the power of an Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the general plan is to just not bring him up or show him in art. If folks want him to be there and deal with the issues he brings-up that's more for their table. But I don't think 3e is going to bring him up nor is it going to go out of its way to explicilty de-canon him.<br /> <br /> On why someone like Havesh, the Sun picks people he htinks he'd like. Whether folks follow through in ways the Sun likes is another matter. Seeing the entire point of the late First Age's Sun turning his back on his Chosen, I think that he can regret some of his picks is perfectly fine. Or that he makes picks we might not agree with due to well, a god working in mysterious ways. What qualifies someone for Solar Exaltation or not is ultimatley up to the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T14:15:53-07:00","id":1505500,"title":"","content":"That first post (from more than a year ago by a person who has not logged on in about as long) is informed more by the reductive internet version of Havesh.<br /> <br /> Havesh killed the people at the pinnacle of his society, who were the greatest beneficiaries of the system that left him crushed and despised in his mortal life, in exchange for large sums of money. He did this to gratify himself in defiance of how he has once been discriminated against.<br /> <br /> The exception was a guy with a top place in the caste system who was socializing with Havesh while in disguise and went out of his way to cruelly mistreat another casteless person begging in the street.<br /> <br /> The story Havesh is given in Caste Book: Night has implications that his trajectory can end up in the direction of being a champion for the most downtrodden parts of his society, even if his methods and motives for doing so would likely be fairly mercenary.<br /> <br /> Havesh was ruthless and self-interested, but he didn't direct those traits against the already disenfranchised around him.<br /> <br /> In terms of the current Edition, he actually comes across as less ruthless than Yurgen conducting sieges against cities by catapulting in pigs that have been contaminated with boneus eruptus.<br /> <br /> The character of the Unconconqered Sun probably shouldn't be seen as precluding Chosen with a ruthless disposition and great ambition, so long as they don't have the most atrocious personalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T18:04:51-07:00","id":1505519,"title":"","content":"The main reason not to bring back Havesh this edition is that Yane's already got some fairly interesting threats to the establishment in Adversaries of the Righteous.<br /> <br /> Fehim's got more of a role in things rather than just being the idiot who'll sell his soul eventually and the Darienites are pretty cool for a Yozi Cult. I think a second Celestial Exalt in the city fighting the status quo risks it feeling a bit overcrowded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-17-2023, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T18:45:08-07:00","id":1505521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1505343#post1505343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we should be too hard on the Sun for picking Havesh. (He deserves flack for abandoning Creation instead!)<br /> <br /> He isn't the Maidens, so he presumably can't predict the future all that well. He can look into a person's heart as they are right now, but he doesn't interview them to ask what specific actions they'll take if he gives them power. To some extent, I think he (and everyone who isn't the Maidens) has to just trust. Sometimes, you get Lyta or Havesh, but sometimes you get Harmonious Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, even in both of the Caste books where they were introduced, both Lyta and Havesh were given setup for character arcs that could see them change and develop. For example Lyta starts off hating all of the Dragon Blooded and wanting to execute them. Then you see at the end of the book she has Dragon Blooded followers and has come to the conclusion that Dragon Blooded aren't inherently evil, rather it's the Realm that is evil and corruptive and the Dragon Blooded living it are bad because they grew up in it, not because they were born that way. Dragon Blooded from places other than the Realm don't need to be killed, and she has a moment where she's even considering that those Dragon Blooded born in the Realm don't necessarily need to be killed, provided that they reject the Realm's actions and beliefs.<br /> <br /> And then as Isator points out, you see a bit of a similar moment with Havesh where the spark of heroism is possibly ignited.<br /> <br /> Honestly one of my favorite things about the old Solar Caste books was that each book had one Solar who embodied the negative stereotypes that the Immaculate Order had concerning the Solars: Fehim, Lyta, Havesh, etc. of those, I think Fehim was the only one who wasn't necessarily given a starting step towards a more positive character arc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T05:58:42-07:00","id":1505535,"title":"","content":"Most uncomfortable thing about Havesh's chapters to me is how casually he talks about his older sister being forced into prostitution (like literally with a pimp who'd beat her up if she stopped to talk to him). I don't think anything before or since has implied Varang's this-is-what-we-think-a-caste-system-is is that fucked up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-17-2023, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T08:17:40-07:00","id":1505545,"title":"","content":"I mostly wouldn't expect Havesh to be referenced again because he's not really a prominent enough personage of the setting or writing to be worth it over any new Solars a person might write, and doesn't have much significance beyond meme status.<br /> <br /> I'm really more concerned with using him as a reference point to what some of the parameters for the Solar Exalted might be, and how such choices might be seen in terms other than the Unconquered Sun being totally callous or indifferent.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that there's <i>nothing</i> a bit callous in the act of empowering somebody who might prove ruthless with it, just that it's kind of a nuanced subject.<br /> <br /> Although this is another point where I'll reiterate that the books seem to have always maintained a through line that the people who become Solars were not super prominent or successful before being Chosen, don't seem to ever be in positions where they already have oppressive authority over others, and seem to frequently end up as people who don't abuse their powers to add to the suffering of the already downtrodden.<br /> <br /> Although even that would likely end up having certain nuances as the conflicts they engage with grow. If you make war against the Realm, how deserving are the soldiers of the legions of death? They're not exactly conscripts (not yet, at least), but nor are they totally self-determined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T10:26:58-07:00","id":1506424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1505535#post1505535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most uncomfortable thing about Havesh's chapters to me is how casually he talks about his older sister being forced into prostitution (like literally with a pimp who'd beat her up if she stopped to talk to him). I don't think anything before or since has implied Varang's this-is-what-we-think-a-caste-system-is is that fucked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Caste and Aspect books for you, often overly edgy with moments that are inconsistent with the setting and fall into very stereotypical tropes. <br /> Though part of the issue here is that Varang's 'caste' system is presented first and foremost as impenetrable to outsiders rather than making sense to them as the only system they know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T16:35:21-07:00","id":1506801,"title":"","content":"The big thing that's missing about Varang and its system is what the incentives are for people to actually follow it rather than making stuff up when it suits them because state violence only goes so far when admitting that you don't know when your child was born condemns them to a life of hardship.<br /> <br /> I assume this adherence has some basis in religion, but it's genuinely pretty vague on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T06:18:51-07:00","id":1506845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1506801#post1506801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big thing that's missing about Varang and its system is what the incentives are for people to actually follow it rather than making stuff up when it suits them because state violence only goes so far when admitting that you don't know when your child was born condemns them to a life of hardship.<br /> <br /> I assume this adherence has some basis in religion, but it's genuinely pretty vague on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there was the fact correct use of even mortal astrology offered all kinds of benefits that were pretty much the factor behind Varang's convoluted caste system in the first place. But i guess that take strongly depends on what kind of mechanical impact mortal astrology might have or not in 3rd edition with the retooling of thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T18:05:52-07:00","id":1506901,"title":"","content":"The mechanical benefits were an after the fact inclusion and quite frankly a distraction from understanding the Varangians and what they believe because they don't and <b>have never </b>done exactly whatever the stars tell them, it makes it abundantly clear in both Scavenger Sons and Compass South that a noble's child and a commoner's child assigned to the same caste enter at different levels with different skill sets.<br /> <br /> This is probably because the upper classes would probably start to tear the system down if their children were regularly forced into menial or degrading roles through mere accident of birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-30-2023, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T11:21:07-07:00","id":1506963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1506801#post1506801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big thing that's missing about Varang and its system is what the incentives are for people to actually follow it rather than making stuff up when it suits them because state violence only goes so far when admitting that you don't know when your child was born condemns them to a life of hardship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think violence is necessary so much as people invested in the system having the means to proscribe access on their terms. You don't need to smack somebody around, you just need to close the door on them when they come asking if their child can have an apprenticeship. Are Varangians better equipped than most historical people to organise in opposition to such mistreatment?<br /> <br /> I think historically the thing that has propped such systems up is not constant enforcement through violence so much as limited means to organise; to communicate a time and a venue to people with discontent, and to have a means of providing both.<br /> <br /> In which case it isn't a question of what incentivizes people to participate so much as what drives those in possession of authority to utilise such a restriction of access, and I think it can be enough there for somebody to think that this accomplishes purposes of maintaining certain hierarchies and imposing what is perceived as a most orderly society.<br /> <br /> Within the necessary allowances of being a pulp fantasy setting where a bit more priority is given to what is dramatic rather than what holds up with sufficient logic.<br /> <br /> As for children, I don't know; I think throughout much of history, most people have loved their children, but their love is constrained by material concerns. If you're a farmer, you endeavour to a larger number of children because that bestows social status and more hands for the fields and the household, and never mind that there will be more of them than can inherit anything from you. It's not worth going to the effort of rising against systems that render extraneous people destitute, even if you could figure out an alternative.<br /> <br /> And perhaps there are larger things going on behind the casteless, as happened with Havesh whose mother could not make even a token attempt to report on his time of birth because she was so inebriated. I'd say that for most people who are well-to-do and have it together, it's very uncommon to lack such knowledge because of the social stigma, and in cases where it is lacking it's not unknown to fabricate details (but perhaps fear and lack of confidence means they admit the truth often enough), and it's really a thing that arises most often from the people who are flawed or too beaten down to really care that much. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T14:39:25-07:00","id":1506991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1506963#post1506963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Varangians better equipped than most historical people to organise in opposition to such mistreatment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think there's good reasons why nobody's attempted to stratify society by time of birth IRL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the necessary allowances of being a pulp fantasy setting where a bit more priority is given to what is dramatic rather than what holds up with sufficient logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>My dog in this fight is my ability to portray a Varangian who didn't spend their entire life outside of its system. Scavenger Sons did an adequate job presenting Varang as an incomprehensibly alien (dare I say Orientalist?) place from a perspective of the player characters who are assumed to be outsiders getting drawn into intrigue in a foreign land but I don't feel adequately equipped to grapple with it in any real depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-30-2023, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T12:08:11-07:00","id":1507066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1506991#post1506991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think there's good reasons why nobody's attempted to stratify society by time of birth IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because real life doesn't operate by the dramatic licence that things in a pulp fantasy setting does.<br /> <br /> Like, we can put in as many implications as we can think of derived from gods and Exalted, and it won't change the fact that even the most verisimilitudinous part of the setting is ultimately a lot more neat and driven by theme than something in reality would be.<br /> <br /> (This is also the answer to a lot of people's curious complaints about the society on the Caul.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T18:17:32-07:00","id":1507089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1507066#post1507066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because real life doesn't operate by the dramatic licence that things in a pulp fantasy setting does.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's the world building equivalent of &quot;it's magic, I ain't gonna explain shit&quot; and it can justify any set of social conditions no matter how politically biased, sexist or racist.<br /> <br /> Like for example, your fantasy world where gods regularly communicate with their worshipers can have Mesoamerican coded people labouring under the mistaken belief that the sun will destroy the world if not offered a fresh human heart every afternoon, that's very pulp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-31-2023, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T12:52:33-07:00","id":1507198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1506991#post1506991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think there's good reasons why nobody's attempted to stratify society by time of birth IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Isator pointed out, actual stratification of status is inherited with socioeconomic status. Astrology and time of birth determine general job category, but your parents' wealth determines whether you're trained to be a skilled artisan or an unskilled porter, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Still, personally I might consider rewriting Varangia to only separate job category by day, not by time. A pre-industrial, post-apocalyptic society can only have so many specialized job categories anyway. Do they really need more than 425 of them? If they had more than 425, would that really leave room for the status-based subdivisions that keep noble-born people on top? Havesh's story would still make sense if his mother woke up from a hangover, looked at her newborn she didn't rememer having, and wondered what the heck day it was.<br /> <br /> As for the child prostitution, it's horrific but unremarkable by real-world standards. And I think that a noble child born on the same day would become a luxury courtesan (and not have to work until after puberty) or a pimp or procurer, instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 04-02-2023, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T17:08:56-07:00","id":1507241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1507198#post1507198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Isator pointed out, actual stratification of status is inherited with socioeconomic status. Astrology and time of birth determine general job category, but your parents' wealth determines whether you're trained to be a skilled artisan or an unskilled porter, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat was me. Your career being determined by your hour of birth is still social stratification especially if your hour of birth going unreported is tantamount to exile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, personally I might consider rewriting Varangia to only separate job category by day, not by time. A pre-industrial, post-apocalyptic society can only have so many specialized job categories anyway. Do they really need more than 425 of them? If they had more than 425, would that really leave room for the status-based subdivisions that keep noble-born people on top? Havesh's story would still make sense if his mother woke up from a hangover, looked at her newborn she didn't rememer having, and wondered what the heck day it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the exact hour being important is derived from the birth charts of Vedic astrology and the rigid system is a reference to the Hindu caste system with the Outcastes as the Dalit, which is part of why the presentation of Varang makes me slightly uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think reducing the overall number of roles would allow for some definition rather than giving no details and insisting it's just too complicated to explain it all with the available space and thus not even making a token effort. They're not <i>aliens</i>. \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T12:23:48-07:00","id":1507305,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there's anything that supports or contradicts the idea that Varangian castes are not made exclusive to the particular star charts that might be assigned by them. Which is to say that there can be multiple times of day a person could be born at in which they get designated a cooper.<br /> <br /> Which is historically distinct in term from a carpenter in ways that might even have legal backing, in spite of the fact that carpenters tend to make barrels and coopers tend to do a bit of additional woodworking on the side, whether it's permitted or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T13:21:56-07:00","id":1508067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1506901#post1506901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanical benefits were an after the fact inclusion and quite frankly a distraction from understanding the Varangians and what they believe because they don't and <b>have never </b>done exactly whatever the stars tell them, it makes it abundantly clear in both Scavenger Sons and Compass South that a noble's child and a commoner's child assigned to the same caste enter at different levels with different skill sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this does raise the question of what the Varangians <i>believe</i> about how practically effective the system is.<br /> <br /> (I'm not sure I'd even call this a religious belief, since... to them, it's not really religion? It's how they believe things are. If your star charts say X you will be good at Y, in the same way that people in the real world might say that someone who grows to six-foot-ten might be good at basketball. But even moreso, since I think they believe the star charts actually predict that you will be as happy as you could be doing Y.)<br /> <br /> If they believe the star charts genuinely work, then they might adhere to them because they believe that their children will genuinely have a happier life following what the stars say. Wealthy people might bend the rules but there's a surprising lack of discussion of people outright <i>forging</i> the time of birth, which is what you'd expect them to do if they thought the whole system was hokum.<br /> <br /> This doesn't explain why anyone would willingly admit to not knowing their child's time of birth, which cannot possibly benefit them even if you strictly believe in the effectiveness of the star charts, but it could be limited to parents who are terminally negligent (as Havesh's backstory suggests) - there are unfortunately absolutely parents like that in the real world, who wouldn't even bother with the slight effort it would take to come up with a plausible lie. Or to births that happen in situations where there's no way the parent can credibly claim to know the time of birth, or when they die in childbirth and nobody who cares enough to lie was present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T17:08:01-07:00","id":1508085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1473884-is-havesh-the-vanisher-still-a-thing?p=1508067#post1508067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't explain why anyone would willingly admit to not knowing their child's time of birth, which cannot possibly benefit them even if you strictly believe in the effectiveness of the star charts, but it could be limited to parents who are terminally negligent (as Havesh's backstory suggests) - there are unfortunately absolutely parents like that in the real world, who wouldn't even bother with the slight effort it would take to come up with a plausible lie. Or to births that happen in situations where there's no way the parent can credibly claim to know the time of birth, or when they die in childbirth and nobody who cares enough to lie was present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's a big part of my issue, if that's all outcasts are then quite frankly they're taking up way too much space because with those elements Havesh's story plays out basically the same place pretty much <b>anywhere</b> in Creation, with the possible exception of Paragon.<br /> <br /> Edit: to clarify, the Scavenger Sons entry for Varang predominantly exists to tell two stories a culture clash with the invariably foreign player characters and to tell stories about ostracisation with the outcasts. If we treat what caste book Night says about Yane seriously I'd argue they're completely unnecessary because we're given an example of a low-station entertainer being forced into underaged sex work with a constant threat of violence hanging over her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-12-2023, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}